<div class="container" style="padding-top: 48px; padding-bottom: 48px;">
  <h1>About Blueprint</h1>

  <section style="padding-top: 24px;">
    <h2>What is Blueprint?</h2>
    <p style="color: var(--color-text-muted); max-width: 700px; margin-bottom: 16px;">
      Blueprint is an open-source web application for defining, sharing, and reproducing
      development environments as code. Think of it as "dotfiles as a service" with a
      web interface and a CLI for bootstrapping new machines.
    </p>
    <p style="color: var(--color-text-muted); max-width: 700px; margin-bottom: 16px;">
      Every time you set up a new machine, you rebuild from scratch. You install packages,
      configure dotfiles, set environment variables, enable services. Blueprint makes this
      process declarative: define it once, share it via URL, reproduce it anywhere.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Sample Blueprint YAML</h2>
    <pre><code>name: "Arch Linux Hyprland Desktop"
description: "Full Arch Linux setup with Hyprland, Waybar, and dev tools"

packages:
  - name: hyprland
    category: pacman
  - name: waybar
    category: pacman
  - name: kitty
    category: pacman
  - name: neovim
    category: pacman
  - name: fuzzel
    category: pacman
  - name: mise
    category: aur

dotfiles:
  - name: Hyprland Config
    target_path: ~/.config/hypr/hyprland.conf
    content: |
      # Hyprland configuration
      monitor=,preferred,auto,1
      $terminal = kitty
      $menu = fuzzel

environment:
  EDITOR: nvim
  BROWSER: firefox
  TERMINAL: kitty

services:
  - name: docker
    enabled: true
  - name: bluetooth
    enabled: true</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>CLI Usage</h2>
    <pre><code># Install the CLI
gem install blueprint-cli

# Pull a blueprint and apply it
blueprint apply @synth/arch-hyprland

# Export as a shell script
blueprint export @synth/arch-hyprland --format shell > setup.sh

# Download the raw YAML
blueprint download @synth/arch-hyprland > my-blueprint.yml</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>API</h2>
    <pre><code># List public blueprints
curl https://blueprint.dev/api/v1/blueprints

# Get a specific blueprint
curl https://blueprint.dev/api/v1/blueprints/arch-hyprland

# Download as shell script
curl https://blueprint.dev/api/v1/blueprints/arch-hyprland/download_script

# Download as YAML
curl https://blueprint.dev/api/v1/blueprints/arch-hyprland/download_yaml</code></pre>
  </section>

